    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) and Its Defences',
         body=None,
         narration="Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains server-side request forgery, S S R F, and its defences, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] Some features make a server fetch a web address that a customer gives it. [[slnc 300]] But the server sits inside the company network, where it can reach things that no customer can. [[slnc 300]] So the customer only has to give an address that points inside. [[slnc 600]] Think of a courier who will collect a parcel from any address you write down. [[slnc 300]] Write the address of a locked room inside the courier's own warehouse, and the courier walks straight in, because the courier has the keys. [[slnc 600]] Our example is an online store that imports product images."),
