    dict(key='08-costs', kind='bullets', title='What It Costs',
         body=['An allow-list of hosts is safer, but needs upkeep', 'Some customers use private addresses on purpose', 'Looking names up yourself is more work', 'Rules for outgoing traffic still matter', 'The metadata service needs its own protection'],
         narration="Nothing is free. [[slnc 400]] Here is what the defences cost. [[slnc 500]] A fixed list of allowed hosts is safer than a list of blocked ones, but someone has to keep it up to date. [[slnc 500]] Some customers point at private addresses on purpose, and they will be refused. [[slnc 500]] Looking up the name yourself, and connecting to the address you checked, is more work than calling a library. [[slnc 500]] Network rules that stop the server's outgoing traffic still matter, as a second wall. [[slnc 500]] And the cloud metadata service needs its own protection, like the newer version that asks for a token first."),
